# nextcloud-exelearning .distignore
#
# Patterns listed here are stripped from the Nextcloud distribution
# tarball produced by `make package`. Each line is passed verbatim to
# `rsync --exclude-from=.distignore`, so the syntax matches rsync
# exclude rules (one pattern per line, comments start with `#`).
#
# Mirror any addition you make here in `.gitattributes` so that
# `git archive` exports stay aligned.

# --- Version control & developer metadata --------------------------------
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.distignore
.editorconfig
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
*.swp
.omc
.claude

# --- Dependency directories ---------------------------------------------
# Nextcloud generates the PSR-4 autoloader from appinfo at install time,
# so the app's own composer vendor/ tree is not needed at runtime.
node_modules
vendor

# --- Build configuration & tooling --------------------------------------
package.json
package-lock.json
composer.json
composer.lock
webpack.config.js
tsconfig.json
vitest.config.ts

# --- Tests, coverage and caches -----------------------------------------
tests
coverage
.cache
.phpunit.cache
.phpunit.result.cache
*.log

# --- Build / release outputs (recreated by `make package`) --------------
build
dist
release
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# --- eXeLearning editor source clone ------------------------------------
# The built editor (downloaded or compiled) lives under js/editor/ and is
# bundled separately; the upstream source clone is never shipped.
exelearning
.editor-version

# --- Project documentation (kept in the repo only) ----------------------
AGENTS.md
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
Makefile

# --- JS source maps and license headers ---------------------------------
# Not required at runtime; keeping them out reduces archive size.
js/*.map
js/*.LICENSE.txt
